{
  "surface": "packages/plugin-api/calls.js#createCalls",
  "description": "Ordered steps of the end of a call. A call has no time limit: it ends by its reply, its cancel or the end of its peer, and the call layer starts no timer. A request step sends a command call (signal true gives it an abort signal), a reply step delivers a reply from the peer, a cancel step aborts the signal of the named request, and a peer-lost step ends the peer with its reason. Each step lists the messages sent, the reports of the call layer (peer-lost, late-reply, open-calls) and the settled outcome of the request that the step watches: {resolved} or {rejected, code}, or null while the call is open. A cancelled call is rejected with cancelled; a call that the end of its peer ends is rejected with command <name> ended: <reason>; a reply that arrives after a cancel is a late reply, reported with its delay and not passed to the call.",
  "cases": [
